+## Maps on phones: a map inside a page is a still that a swipe scrolls past and is used in fullscreen; the tab bar under an expanded map is hidden by one attribute on the root, because `inert` does not stop paint and the bar was taking Exit's taps; Exit carries its word; the Weather picker and the Hotspot Reports map join on the phone tier; the Map Explorer's phone floor is 300 px and it takes the still where it cannot fit; five dropdown lists keep to the visible screen; an Exit drawn by a child that mounts late needed a stand-in; and two app-wide inset fixes are verified on a model only -- 2026-11-22 (map-scroll-on-phones, maintain lane, v1.0.76, shipped in the combined release with family-rollups-and-tree)
 
-**Decision: landed on `main` with no version of its own.** An Improve run with a design pass from saved idea `42b9772c`, the user's report that on phones the page scrolls and the map scrolls too, so a swipe lands on a half-visible map and some on-map buttons end up partly off screen or blocked. Merged into `main` as `758036c7` (build `a96f766a` to `0772a45e` on base `7cf126a6`) with no version bump, changelog entry, tag or release, by the user's choice at the deploy sign-off (run D-40). It reaches every platform in the one combined release with `family-rollups-and-tree` (run D-02), whose record carries the ship, the What's New sentence and the retaken phone pictures that draw a map tab. Run hands-off on Autopilot (D-01). The full record (D-01 to D-40) is `pipeline/map-scroll-on-phones/decisions.md`, and `release-handoff.md` there lists what the combined release owes for this build, the user's device check included.
+**Decision: landed on `main` with no version of its own, then shipped as 1.0.76 with family-rollups-and-tree.** An Improve run with a design pass from saved idea `42b9772c`, the user's report that on phones the page scrolls and the map scrolls too, so a swipe lands on a half-visible map and some on-map buttons end up partly off screen or blocked. Merged into `main` as `758036c7` (build `a96f766a` to `0772a45e` on base `7cf126a6`) with no version bump, changelog entry, tag or release, by the user's choice at the deploy sign-off (run D-40). It reaches every platform in the one combined release with `family-rollups-and-tree` (run D-02), whose record carries the ship, the What's New sentence and the retaken phone pictures that draw a map tab. Run hands-off on Autopilot (D-01). The full record (D-01 to D-40) is `pipeline/map-scroll-on-phones/decisions.md`, and `release-handoff.md` there lists what the combined release owes for this build, the user's device check included.
 
 **What the phone tier does now (D-03, D-07 to D-14).** The phone tier is the media query `(max-width: 640px)` that `lib/useIsPhone.ts` and the stylesheet's established block both read, a width test and nothing else. On it, a map inside a scrolling page is the same live `<SnowMap>` made inert, a still: nothing is remounted, portaled or replaced by a picture. The host wraps its map subtree in one `.sr-map-still-body`, inert and taking no pointer while still, so a swipe that starts on the map moves the page and the map moves 0 px; zoom, the base map switcher, the corner row and the cooperative-gestures hint are not drawn, and the credits are drawn open. A press on the still, or on the "Open the map" row under it (`components/ui/FsOpenRow.tsx`, a full-width accent button with one helper line, outside the box that expands), opens the map through the existing class swap in `lib/useMapFullscreen.ts`. A press on a pin opens the map and does not also choose the pin (D-08). Exit is the same toggle carrying the word "Exit", 44 px tall on every embedded host (D-10). The hook grew by addition only (D-11), so every name a consumer already imported is unchanged; it gained `stillTier`, `still`, `open`, `registerOpener` and `hostClassName`, focus to Exit on open and to the opener after a user exit, and the page's offset restored after a user exit. The form is the one the Family Tree run settled for its tree (this run's D-03), so the maps and the tree read as one pattern, and that build consumes the hook, `FsOpenRow` and the shared classes as one more host. Above 640 px every map surface and list matched the pre-build tree pixel for pixel in the build's readings, with the variance that build-against-build controls also show.
 
